      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'll note that right thumbstick left/right inputs also work to scroll the friends list - but only when the cursor is over the friends list (if you point away, you'll rotate as normal). Suppressing movement in the same way when the quick menu is opened on the right hand would seem to be a good solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-09T04:56:19.240Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you open the quick menu with your left hand, you can scroll your friends list (and other lists) by pointing the laser at the list and using up/down on the right thumbstick. This is very convenient and way easier than trying to hit the scrollbar accurately or using fling navigation. However, if you open the quick menu with your right hand, your left hand movement inputs override this and cause the menu to close instead. Please allow thumbstick scrolling regardless of which hand opened the quick menu.",
